# Throwaway DB-inspection scripts written by audit subagents at the repo root.
# These embed a connection string; one was swept into a commit by `git add -A`
# (2026-07-25). Never let that happen again — the repo is PUBLIC.
/.tmp-*.mjs
/.tmp-*.cjs
/.audit-*.js
/.tokenlens-*.js
/q_audit_tmp.cjs
/*_tmp.cjs

# ── THROWAWAY SCRIPTS: ALLOWLIST THE REPO ROOT, DO NOT DENYLIST NAMES ─────────
# The rules above were a denylist of filename patterns (/.tmp-*.mjs, /.audit-*.js…).
# A denylist of names cannot hold: `.iso2.mjs` was sitting in this repo root and
# `git check-ignore` confirmed it was NOT ignored, so `git add -A` would have committed it.
# These scripts build a Postgres connection string from CN_PW at runtime — committing one
# to a public repo is a credential leak with a filename typo as its only cause.
#
# So: ignore EVERY loose script at the repo root, then un-ignore the handful that belong.
# A new throwaway is safe by default; a real one has to be named on purpose.
/*.mjs
/*.cjs
/*.js
!/next.config.js
!/next.config.mjs
!/postcss.config.js
!/postcss.config.mjs
!/tailwind.config.js
!/eslint.config.js
!/eslint.config.mjs
